			<section class="book-page" id="page-expectation-ch1">
				<div id="chapter-1" style="scroll-margin-top: 5rem;"></div>
				<div id="ch1-expectations" style="scroll-margin-top: 5rem;"></div>

				<div class="page-body-content">
					<div class="chapter-opener-header">
						<div class="chapter-opener-num">Chapter 1</div>
						<h2 class="chapter-opener-title">Where Could Pain Be Coming&nbsp;From?</h2>
						<div class="chapter-opener-divider"></div>
					</div>

					<div class="chapter-content is-first-page">
						<p>Burning mouth pain has multiple biological root causes. It can stem from central neuropathic injury, peripheral small-fiber neuropathy, hormonal shifts, autoimmune conditions, or localized epithelial and dental triggers. This book is specifically and rigorously an investigation into one specific, overlooked variable: the acid-triggered and tubule leak mechanism discovered through my personal N=1 journey. I do not know how many sufferers share this exact mechanism, and we urgently need large-scale clinical trials to establish the true epidemiological proportion of patients who can be helped. What we do know is that acid sensitivity can be systematically tested through temporary dietary restriction, but it cannot be assumed to cure every single reader.</p>
						<p>Depending on where you are in your diagnostic odyssey, you might enter this book with desperate hope or profound skepticism. Both responses are entirely rational. When you have spent years cycling through dental operatories, neurology clinics, and rheumatology offices only to be told that your oral tissues look pristine and the sensation must be psychosomatic, skepticism is a protective defense. This book is not written to offer an emotional bypass. It is an investigative laboratory: a transparent, peer-reviewed framework designed to help you methodically isolate variables and uncover whether your pain follows electrochemical laws.</p>
						<p>The goal is clarity, not complacency. By working through this clinical framework, you will either discover the primary mechanical or biochemical triggers keeping your pain alive, or you will definitively rule out the acid variable and move on to other targeted therapies without lingering ambiguity. We begin with the evidence, unvarnished and exact.</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="page-number-footer">
					<span>1</span>
				</div>
