					<div class="chapter-content">
						<h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 800; color: #581c87; margin-bottom: 0.65rem;">Anatomical Sensation &amp; Receptor Matrix</h3>
						<p style="font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; color: #334155; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
							Standard dental exams inspect mucosal color, looking for red patches, white plaques, or open ulcers. But the pain of burning mouth lives below macroscopic eyesight. The matrix below connects each commonly reported patient sensation to its anatomical target and underlying receptor trigger:
						</p>

						<div class="bms-matrix-table-wrap" style="overflow-x: auto; margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem;">
							<table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-family: 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 0.76rem; line-height: 1.4; text-align: left;">
