							<span class="book-title-header-label">Acid-Triggered Burning Mouth</span>
							<span class="chapter-header-label">Chapter 4: Who Patients Go and See, and What They Ask and Say</span>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="chapter-content">
						<ol class="chapter-list" start="6" style="margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
							<li style="margin-bottom: 0.65rem;">
								<strong>6. The Gastroenterologist (GI Specialist):</strong> <em>"Your upper endoscopy shows mild gastritis, but no severe esophageal ulceration. Continue the acid blockers."</em> (Patients note that blocking stomach acid does not stop oral burning triggered by dietary acids or oral biofilm fermentation.)
							</li>
							<li style="margin-bottom: 0.65rem;">
								<strong>7. The Endocrinologist:</strong> <em>"Your TSH and free T4 thyroid levels are within range, and your HbA1c shows no diabetes. Your endocrine system cannot explain why your tongue is burning."</em>
							</li>
							<li style="margin-bottom: 0.65rem;">
								<strong>8. The Allergist / Immunologist:</strong> <em>"All environmental allergy prick tests are negative. We can order dental patch testing to see if you are allergic to dental resins, metals, or acrylates."</em> (Patch tests frequently return negative, proving the issue is biochemical and physical rather than an IgE-mediated allergic response.)
							</li>
							<li style="margin-bottom: 0.65rem;">
								<strong>9. The Periodontist:</strong> <em>"Your periodontal probing depths are normal at 2 to 3 millimeters with minimal bleeding on probing. Deep root scaling and curettage won't stop tongue burning."</em> (Standard probing probes gum attachment, but does not test microscopic cement gaps under crown margins.)
							</li>
							<li style="margin-bottom: 0.65rem;">
								<strong>10. The Psychiatrist / Clinical Psychologist:</strong> <em>"Since all physical medical examinations have ruled out organic pathology, your chronic pain is somatic symptom disorder driven by health anxiety. We should focus on cognitive behavioral therapy and antidepressants."</em>
							</li>
						</ol>

						<h3 style="font-size: 1.12rem; font-weight: 800; color: #581c87; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">The Equipment Resolution Barrier</h3>
						<p style="font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.7; color: #1e293b; margin-bottom: 0.85rem;">
							These encounters are deeply demoralizing not because doctors are uncaring, but because medicine operates under an <strong>equipment resolution barrier</strong>. Conventional clinical tools were designed to find gross macroscopic pathology: a visible ulcer, a decaying cavitation, a bleeding tumor, or an abnormal blood cell count.
						</p>

						<p style="font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.7; color: #334155; margin: 0;">
							When pain is driven by sub-micron Acid-Sensing Ion Channels (ASIC3) gating open at pH 6.7, or by a 2-micron dental cement washout feeding anaerobic lactic acid bacteria, the gross clinical exam returns a "clean" bill of health. In the next chapter, we look at the hard statistics that prove how widespread and severe this unmeasured crisis truly is.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>

