							<div class="stat-page-desc" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.85rem;">
								<p>
									Because the oral tissue looks completely pink and healthy under macroscopic examination, diagnosis presents a profound clinical challenge for medical and dental professionals.
								</p>
								<p>
									Clinical surveys (Klasser et al. 2011; Kohorst et al. 2014 <a href="#src-27" class="cite-ref">[27]</a>) show that patients spend an average search time of over 26 months (2.2 years) seeking clarity.
								</p>
								<p>
									During this diagnostic journey, individuals attend an average of six or more clinical appointments across four distinct clinicians before an accurate diagnosis is reached.
								</p>
								<p>
									When macroscopic tests return normal, clinicians are systematically trained to rule out visible disease, making specialized trigeminal neuro-functional screening essential.
								</p>
