						<p>Trusting my engineering data, I insisted on sectioning and removing crown #19. Beneath the old crown, the reality was unmistakable: the cement had washed out, revealing <strong>three separate pockets of recurrent anaerobic decay</strong> and soft necrotic dentin generating continuous organic acid right against the lingual nerve path.</p>

