					<div class="chapter-content">
						<div style="margin-bottom: 1.2rem;">
							<h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; color: #0f172a; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">Step 3: Find a Dentist to Test and Seal Leaking Teeth</h3>
							<p style="margin-bottom: 0.35rem;"><strong>What this step is:</strong> Move from temporary dietary changes to lasting mechanical protection by partnering with a dentist.</p>
							<p style="margin-bottom: 0.35rem;"><strong>Actions: Go see a dentist, or find a dentist who can:</strong></p>
							<ul style="margin: 0.2rem 0 0.6rem 1.35rem; padding: 0; line-height: 1.65; list-style-type: disc;">
								<li style="margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">Paint a reversible desensitizing liquid (such as Gluma or Tokuyama Shield Force Plus) onto exposed root necks or suspect crown margins to pinpoint the exact leak.</li>
								<li style="margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">Examine teeth with fiber-optic transillumination (FOTI) and high magnification to spotlight hidden hairline cracks.</li>
								<li style="margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">Trace filling and crown edges with fine dental explorers to spot washed-out cement seams around older dental work.</li>
								<li>Seal worn root notches with protective dental resin and patch leaking crown margins permanently.</li>
							</ul>
							<p style="margin-bottom: 1.1rem;"><strong>What you will discover:</strong> Microscopic pores and microscopic cement gaps become physically blocked. Acid cannot seep inward to trigger the living nerve fibers inside your teeth, and the referred burning finally stops at the source.</p>

							<h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; color: #0f172a; margin-top: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">Step 4: Bring Back Normal Foods and Reclaim Your Life</h3>
							<p style="margin-bottom: 0.35rem;"><strong>What this step is:</strong> Return to eating a wide variety of healthy, delicious meals without restarting the oral burn.</p>
							<p style="margin-bottom: 0.35rem;"><strong>Actions:</strong></p>
							<ul style="margin: 0.2rem 0 0.6rem 1.35rem; padding: 0; line-height: 1.65; list-style-type: disc;">
								<li style="margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">Begin slowly adding back fresh whole-food fruits, balanced carbohydrates, and family meals once dental leaks are sealed.</li>
								<li style="margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">Monitor your mouth comfort over 3 to 5 days after each new food group.</li>
								<li>Maintain gentle, non-acidic oral hygiene habits to keep restorations clean and gums protected.</li>
							</ul>
							<p style="margin-bottom: 0.85rem;"><strong>What you will discover:</strong> Because the physical doorways into your tooth nerves are firmly sealed, ordinary food acids and daily chewing cannot penetrate into living pulp tissue. You can enjoy meals with friends and family without fear.</p>
						</div>

						<h3>Why This Sequence Resolves Patient Confusion</h3>
						<p><strong>Eliminates the "Carnivore Forever" Fear:</strong> The reader clearly sees that restrictive dieting is Step 1 (The Fire Extinguisher), not a lifetime sentence. It gives you a clear end goal: seal the teeth so you can eat normally&nbsp;again.</p>
						<p><strong>Reframes Tracking as an Actionable Investigation:</strong> Instead of feeling like passive symptom journaling, documenting becomes Step 2: gathering the exact coordinates needed to perform Step 3 (the dental repair).</p>
						<p><strong>Restores Agency to Dental Visits:</strong> Patients understand why previous dental visits failed (going in during an active 10/10 firestorm with diffuse symptoms) and how to approach them effectively now: calm the fire first, then test specific teeth with reversible chairside sealers.</p>
