					<div class="chapter-content">
						<h3>Records to Request from Your Doctors and Dentists</h3>
						<p>Under federal and provincial health information laws (such as HIPAA in the United States and PIPEDA in Canada), you have an unconditional legal right to obtain complete copies of your health records. When consulting new providers, do not rely on oral summaries. Formally request this complete clinical dossier:</p>

						<div class="book-callout" style="margin-top: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.95rem;">
							<div class="book-callout-text">
								<p><strong>From Your Dental Practice (Request Digital Copies):</strong><br />
								1. <strong>Full Mouth Radiographic Series (FMX) and Bitewings:</strong> High-resolution digital DICOM or uncompressed JPEG files (not low-res printouts on paper).<br />
								2. <strong>Periodontal Charting History:</strong> Complete 6-point probing depth records, gingival recession measurements, and bleeding on probing (BOP) indices across all past 3 to 5 years.<br />
								3. <strong>Complete Restorative Operative Notes:</strong> Detailed records specifying the exact brand, adhesive system (total-etch vs. self-etch), composite resin type, and date of placement for every filling, crown, onlay, and implant.<br />
								4. <strong>Occlusal and Wear Documentation:</strong> Diagnostic intraoral scans (iTero, TRIOS) or notes regarding facet wear, abfraction notches, or bruxism patterns.<br />
								5. <strong>Material Safety Data Sheets (MSDS):</strong> Specific dental cement and bonding agents used during recent restorative seating.</p>
							</div>
						</div>

						<div class="book-callout" style="margin-bottom: 0.95rem;">
							<div class="book-callout-text">
								<p><strong>From Your Medical Physicians (ENT, Primary Care, Neurologist):</strong><br />
								1. <strong>Comprehensive Micronutrient Blood Panels:</strong> Serum ferritin, Vitamin B12 (and methylmalonic acid), Serum Folate, Vitamin D, Zinc, and Copper.<br />
								2. <strong>Metabolic and Endocrine Labs:</strong> Fasting blood glucose, HbA1c, full Thyroid panel (TSH, Free T3, Free T4, TPO antibodies), and morning cortisol.<br />
								3. <strong>Autoimmune Serology:</strong> Anti-SSA/Ro and Anti-SSB/La (Sjögren's Syndrome), ANA titer, and Rheumatoid Factor.<br />
								4. <strong>Gastrointestinal Reports:</strong> Endoscopy findings (esophagitis, hiatal hernia, Barrett's), 24-hour pH-impedance monitoring, or Pepsin saliva test results.<br />
								5. <strong>Clinical Consultation Reports:</strong> Exact dictated specialist visit notes, differential diagnostic impressions, and formal prescription history.</p>
							</div>
						</div>
