						<div class="chapter-opener-divider"></div>
					</div>

					<div class="chapter-content is-first-page">
						<p style="line-height: 1.68; color: #334155; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; text-wrap: pretty;">
							Use this comprehensive clinical diagnostic questionnaire to map your symptom profile, identify triggers, and establish an actionable record. You can select your answers directly on this page; your entries are preserved locally and can be printed or shared with your dental and medical&nbsp;providers.
						</p>

																		<!-- Emergency Medical Safety Warning Card -->
						<div id="ch19-emergency-warning" class="quiz-book-card bms-emergency-alert-card" style="margin-bottom: 1.25rem; padding: 0.25rem 1.45rem 1.35rem; background: #fef2f2; border: 1.5px solid #ef4444; border-radius: 10px;">
							<h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700; color: #991b1b; margin: 0 0 0.45rem; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem;">
								<span>Emergency Clinical Safety Warning</span>
							</h3>
							<p style="color: #7f1d1d; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 0.45rem;">
								<strong>Emergency Notice:</strong> If you experience sudden chest pain, shortness of breath, sudden facial droop, slurred speech, or acute throat or tongue swelling, <strong>call 911 or go to an emergency room immediately</strong>. If you are ever unsure whether your symptoms are an emergency, always call 911 or seek urgent emergency medical evaluation.
							</p>
							<p style="color: #991b1b; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 0;">
								This clinical self-assessment is designed exclusively for the systematic documentation and analysis of chronic, persistent intraoral burning sensations. It does not replace medical evaluation. Always consult a licensed physician, oral medicine specialist, or dentist for professional diagnosis and&nbsp;treatment.
							</p>
						</div>

						<!-- Section A0: Clinical Safety Triage (Red-Flag Screener) -->
						<div class="quiz-book-card" style="margin-bottom: 1.25rem; padding: 0.25rem 1.45rem 1.35rem; background: #fff5f5; border: 1.5px solid #feb2b2; border-radius: 10px;">
							<h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700; color: #991b1b; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem;">
								<span>Initial Clinical Safety Triage (Red-Flag Warning Signs)</span>
							</h3>
							<p style="color: #7f1d1d; line-height: 1.55; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
								These specific clinical signs do not fit typical Primary Burning Mouth Syndrome. If any apply, they require prompt professional evaluation by an oral surgeon, ENT specialist, or physician before pursuing at-home self-management:
							</p>
							<div class="bms-grid-2col" style="font-size: 1.0625rem; color: #18181b;">
								<label class="bms-check-label"><input type="checkbox" name="redflag_unilateral" class="bms-input-persist" /> <span>Burning or pain strictly on one side of the mouth</span></label>
