					<div class="chapter-content">
						<h3>Section 2: Modern Solutions for Old Fillings, Crown Margins &amp; Micro-Leaks</h3>
						<p>Over 5 to 15 years, composite resins shrink, adhesive bonding layers hydrolyze under salivary enzymes, and crown cement margins dissolve. These sub-micron perimeter crevasses allow saliva and bacterial acids to siphon continuously down to pulpal afferents. Modern restorative dentistry offers targeted solutions to reseal or replace compromised restoration&nbsp;boundaries:</p>

