						<p><strong>Applying Tokuyama Shield Force Plus for Aging Fillings:</strong> For older composite resin fillings, degraded amalgam margins, or worn cervical restorations where bonding agents have slowly hydrolyzed, dentists apply advanced self-etching resin sealants like <strong>Tokuyama Shield Force Plus</strong> <a href="#src-38" class="cite-ref">[38]</a>. Unlike surface varnishes that wash away in saliva within hours, Tokuyama utilizes 3D-SR monomer technology that penetrates into microscopic perimeter gaps around aging fillings, polymerizing into a durable, acid-resistant physical seal. If painting Tokuyama across older fillings immediately reduces your daily burning flares, you obtain direct clinical proof that sub-micron margin degradation was fueling the&nbsp;fire.</p>

